  "note": [
    "Scripture authority is the 1962 Amharic Bible (UBS; NT revised 2003). Its New Testament is on disk whole (ebible mirror gracious-tech/fetch_collection, bibles/amh_amh). The mirror carries no Old Testament, so OT quotations reuse the wording of an already-shipped Amharic work where one quotes the same verse (source_file names it) and are otherwise self_rendered in the 1962 register.",
    "A `mined` row was re-measured against the finished text: an exact substring of at least 20 characters of the 1962 NT verse (or 25 of the cited corpus file) inside that block, quote marks aside. Shorter, re-personed or adapted quotations are self_rendered, whatever the translator believed. The mirror bridges some verse ranges into one entry holding only part of their text (e.g. John 3:14-16, Ephesians 6:14-16), and its numbering runs one ahead of the KJV in places (John 1:47 is filed as 1:48, Romans 3:10 as 3:11): such quotations are self_rendered here even where the wording is the 1962 text.",
    "Bunyan's inline margin references are kept inline as printed (Amharic book names, Western digits, no parentheses added). Names follow the pinned glossary drawn from the shipped am children/teens/one-syllable editions; Part 2 minor characters are coined in the same style. AI-translated (job #3714) by fan-out over 17 translators; tag sequence identical to the English per chapter; awaiting native review."
  ],
